WEBVTT

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.570
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.240
<i>With her food supplies running short,</i>

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.400
<i>the Nautilus anchors off an island
to replenish her stores.</i>

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.410
<i>Jean and the others are overjoyed
to walk on land again</i>

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.990
<i>after their long trip in the submarine.</i>

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.370
<i>Jean and the men go hunting,
and return with a baby deer.</i>

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:49.830
<i>Seeing this, Nadia is enraged, and
runs out of camp into the night.</i>

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.070
Up! Everybody up!

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.840
King!

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.130
My dear Nemo...

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:47.350
Is our Senorita still sleeping?

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.350
Still asleep.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:52.900
I don't think she's ever gotten
up on time in her life.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:57.070
Maybe she couldn't sleep for thinking
about Captain Nemo.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:00.280
What does she see in a
middle-aged guy like that?

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:05.700
What's wrong, Jean? You're looking
pretty dismal this morning.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.250
Is it about Nadia?

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:14.420
Yeah, I can't understand her.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:18.130
Why was she so mad
about our hunting?

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.430
This way, no one will
want to talk to her.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:26.810
That's true. Well, you know
what they say.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:32.440
A girl's heart is an eternal riddle to
men. You'll never understand one.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.810
Even you don't know?

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.360
Nope. Not a clue.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:43.490
I wonder if Nadia wants
to live all by herself?

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.330
Well, maybe.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:51.120
But a person cannot live alone,
nor should they live alone.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.960
I'm sure Nadia will realize this soon.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.710
Is that life?

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.590
That's right.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.670
It'll be breakfast soon.
Go wake them up.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.010
Okay.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.350
Nadia...

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:13.850
Nadia!

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.780
Are you up? It'll be breakfast soon.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.570
Hurry and wash up.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.580
You ate it, didn't you?

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:37.840
What do you mean?

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.590
I'm asking you if you ate
that baby deer!

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.300
Go away!

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.680
King! King!

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.430
Why are you so angry?

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:52.480
Nadia!

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:55.310
It was only a baby. Why did
you have to kill it?

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.150
We had to kill it for something to eat.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.770
Why do you have to eat?

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.070
We have to eat to live.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:05.490
Then why can't you just
eat vegetables?

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.950
What about those who can't
eat vegetables?

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.200
There are no such people! They just
haven't tried hard enough.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:15.370
I wonder. Maybe it's you who
hasn't tried hard enough.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:16.420
What did you say?!

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.790
Are you having a family quarrel again?

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.340
No, we're not!

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:25.090
At any rate, I don't want to live
if I have to eat animals.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.510
Why is it wrong to eat them?

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:28.970
Because it's so pitiful!

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:31.140
Why? After all, they're food.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.310
No, not food! They're dead animals!

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.890
Once you cook them, they're
food, aren't they?

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.190
When you look at them, don't
you feel sorry for them?

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.230
Why should l?

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:43.030
Because they were killed to
be eaten by humans!

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:46.030
But we have to kill them
if we want to eat.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.660
That doesn't give you the
right to kill them!

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.490
Don't you feel a little
pity toward them?

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:54.450
I do! That's why we made a
grave for the baby deer.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:01.840
Come on, King. Let's go play.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:05.840
Nadia!

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.550
Ma'am, let's play.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.470
Ma'am?!

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:16.020
I'm sorry. Sister is a little
busy right now.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.600
Later when I've finished making
breakfast, maybe.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:20.940
This is no fun.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:22.610
Let's go!

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:25.740
You're using too much
pepper on the food!

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.490
It tastes better this way.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.410
It just makes it taste more peppery.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:32.070
Be quiet! You always talk too much!

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:34.580
I'm only telling you because I want
my food to taste better.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:37.750
What?! Are you criticizing
my cooking?!

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:40.670
I'm only saying I don't like
my food too hot!

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:44.920
Sanson, girls won't like you
if you criticize too much.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:47.130
She put it all in!

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.760
This is no fun.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:53.510
All I have to do is connect
this circuit to this point?

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.390
Right, the energy is distributed
through that circuit.

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:59.390
What's distribution? What's a circuit?

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:00.600
I see. What about that circuit?

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:01.940
That current flows in this direction.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:03.020
I see.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.610
This is no fun.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:06.440
Let's go!

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:17.500
Say...

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.050
This is no fun.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:33.970
Let's go, King.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:46.150
Wow, what a pretty sight!

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.820
I wonder what's over there?

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.650
Let's go see, King!

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.290
That hurt!

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.620
What's wrong, King?

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:30.090
Railway tracks!

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.420
Wait for me, King!

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.340
Look! I'm a train!

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:41.560
Choo choo... Puff puff...

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:37.700
This is no fun.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.860
Let's go back, King!

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:44.990
London Bridge is falling down!

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:47.370
Falling down! Falling down!

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.540
London Bridge is falling down!

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.750
My fair... What?

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:59.930
There are two railroad tracks.
Which one did we come from?

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:05.260
What should I do?

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.220
Here I go.

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:10.640
That way!

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:25.200
What? The tracks divided again.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.160
Again...

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:32.000
This time, that way!

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:41.380
WHAT?!

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:45.220
Oh, my god!

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:54.560
It's nothing to worry about!

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:41.570
It's okay. There's nothing
to worry about.

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:07.470
Look, King! It's the sea!

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:10.720
That means we're near our Nautilus!

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:18.940
That's not our Nautilus!

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:23.820
Lie down!

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:25.860
That's...

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.490
That's the ship we saw on our island.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:33.200
A ship on which island, little girl?

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:50.850
What do you mean by the ship
you saw? Start talking!

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.220
Come here, little girl.

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:55.350
No!

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.560
Don't be so stubborn.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:00.940
Come now, it's dangerous there.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:02.020
No!

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:18.920
Hey, look out! It's dangerous!

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:26.130
What is that guy trying to do?

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:27.470
There's a small kid with him.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:29.590
Don't let go!

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.890
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:35.850
Hey, what...

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:39.440
King!

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:50.570
I thought I was going to be killed.

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:52.700
Hey! What's up?!

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:56.040
King, let's go!

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:57.620
Hey, stop!

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.620
You all right?

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.670
Yeah, where'd that brat go?

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:03.670
She seems to know
something about us.

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:08.050
King, this way!

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:24.270
They've disappeared.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:26.610
Slippery kid! Now where did they go?

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:27.990
What'll we do?

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:29.490
Let's fire a few rounds to scare them.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:30.950
Okay.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:41.460
Darn it, they got away!

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:43.920
It's only a funny looking cat.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:47.590
That kid has to be around here
someplace. Keep looking!

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:51.630
Where'd she go?

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:54.010
Oh, Nadia...

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:57.140
Rock, Paper, Scissors!

00:15:57.970 --> 00:15:59.980
We won!

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:02.690
Darn it, I lost!

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.440
Everyone knows you always
choose scissors.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:09.110
That's right.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.820
You're so simple!

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:11.490
That's right.

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:13.740
We expect a lot of firewood.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:14.780
That's right.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:17.280
Darn my rotten luck!

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:19.200
Okay, I'll go!

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:21.290
What? The Nautilus?!

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:23.000
Yes, Sir. No question about it.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.290
They don't know about us, do they?

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:29.050
No, they haven't discovered us yet.
We can take them by surprise.

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:31.760
Don't bother. We're sailing out as
soon an we finish refueling.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:32.420
But...

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:36.800
Our mission is reconnaissance, not
fighting. Return to base immediately!

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:37.640
Yes, Sir!

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:42.060
Where'd she go?!

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:47.360
Hey! Orders are to report to base.
We're leaving earlier than planned.

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:48.150
Hurry!

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:49.530
Understood!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:52.150
She's a damn lucky kid!

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:57.280
I've got the worst kind of luck.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:00.990
They've got trains running
on this island?

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:02.580
Nothing but rocks.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.540
Maybe a stone quarry.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.550
It sure is hot!

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:19.810
Jean!

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:21.850
Nadia, you're not mad anymore?

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:23.350
We must find Marie!

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:28.150
We've got to find Marie! I can't find
Marie or King anywhere!

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:41.620
King, where did you go?

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:46.710
Sanson!

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:47.790
What's this?!

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:50.380
Sanson! Sanson! Sanson!

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:53.460
Hey, Sanson! Sanson! Sanson!

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:54.800
Marie...
Hey, Sanson! Sanson! Sanson!

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:56.380
Ga-Ga-Ga...

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:58.050
What do you mean by Ga?

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:00.100
Ga-Ga-Ga...

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:01.600
Gargoyle!

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:07.560
It's that robot tank again.

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:10.980
We'll just have to bust it up again!

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:16.700
Looks like a giant crab.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.870
That's not playing fair!

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.870
What a coward!

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:34.130
Darn it! If I only had my Gratan!

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:35.880
Oh! Lucky!

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:40.430
Won't budge! No luck!

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:42.890
Sanson! Sanson, it's coming!

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:46.680
It's here!

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.060
Lucky!

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:55.980
Of all the luck! That was
my favorite hat!

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:02.070
You lost!

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:05.370
Why don't you try to catch us?!

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:11.790
What's this?!

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:16.460
Stop!

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.680
Lucky!

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:24.180
Bye-bye!
Sayonara!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:32.440
Our luck has run out.

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:33.650
Scissors!

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:38.110
Scissors... scissors... What's
stronger than scissors?!

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:40.200
A rock!

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:50.290
Let's see if you can catch
my super fast ball!

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.750
Lucky! Nice catch!

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:05.220
Rotten pitch!

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.430
Oh, my god! Go away!

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:14.560
Lucky!

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:19.610
Did you find them?

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:23.610
Where in the world have they gone?

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:37.130
The camp's surrounded by the Neo
Atlanteans. What's Nautilus doing?

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:40.380
It's cleverly camouflaged, but they're
camped on the north side

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:42.630
There's a faint magnetic response.

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:44.760
Are you sure? The Neo Atlantis forces?

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:47.760
The possibility is very high.

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:51.020
Okay, get everything ready
for a quick departure.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:51.770
Yes, Sir.

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:54.770
We're shipping out! Get
ready to break camp!

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:57.900
Marie! King!

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:04.820
King!

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.450
What happened? You're so dirty.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:08.780
Where's Marie?

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:13.540
You don't know?!
Weren't you together?

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:19.540
It just won't give up chasing us.

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:49.450
Any luck?

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:50.830
I couldn't find her.

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:52.490
Sanson isn't back either.

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:54.750
If you don't hurry, you'll
be left behind!

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:56.040
That's mean!

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:02.840
Nadia! Nadia! Nadia!

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:06.260
Marie! Where in the world were you?

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:08.760
Ga-Ga-Ga- Gargoyle!

00:22:14.980 --> 00:22:16.430
What's that?!

00:22:21.650 --> 00:22:23.360
It's a Neo Atlantis soldier!

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:27.280
That man is injured!

00:22:27.900 --> 00:22:29.410
Damn!

00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:40.210
What happened?

00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:51.510
No!

00:22:51.970 --> 00:22:56.220
Why?! Why did you shoot him?!
He was hurt!

00:22:56.810 --> 00:22:59.730
He may have shot you.

00:22:59.730 --> 00:23:03.900
That has nothing to do with this!
You murdered him!

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:05.030
Isn't that so?!

00:23:39.810 --> 00:23:43.650
MURDERER!
